<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 3.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 3.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on October 2. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		   P/E	 Close</p>
<p>1  Portman Min	     290.48    1.83</p>
<p>2  Niugini Min	     278.42    3.87</p>
<p>3  Mayne Nickless	  200.68    8.87</p>
<p>4  T N T		     174.10    2.42</p>
<p>5  Adel Bton Cement	126.09    1.74</p>
<p>6  Colonial Coml	   117.49    2.15</p>
<p>7  Herald Rsc		 88.50    1.00</p>
<p>8  Forrestania Gold	 83.33    2.10</p>
<p>9  Westral Forest	   76.09    2.10</p>
<p>10 Cape Range		 70.27    0.26</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p>1  Dominion Min		2.90    0.70</p>
<p>2  Computer Power	    3.32    3.40</p>
<p>3  Premier Inv		 3.49    0.62</p>
<p>4  Parbury Ltd		 5.79    0.68</p>
<p>5  BTR Plc		     5.86    5.40</p>
<p>6  Aust Gold Rsc	     6.58    1.20</p>
<p>7  Pac Mutual Aust	   6.58    2.35</p>
<p>8  OLS Asia Hldgs	    6.89    0.82</p>
<p>9  McIntosh Sec		7.07    0.88</p>
<p>10 Consol Rutile	     7.72    2.18</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
